url: https://investment-journey.streamlit.app

abstract: >-
  An open-source Python and Streamlit investment planning simulator
  for modelling SIPs (systematic investment plans), lump-sum
  investments, contribution step-ups and pauses, withdrawals,
  portfolio rebalancing, goals, historical replay, Monte Carlo
  scenarios, XIRR and tax-aware cash flows. Investment plans are
  represented as timelines of contributions and life events so users
  can examine how timing and financial decisions change long-term
  portfolio outcomes. Journey comparison can attribute differences
  between plans using Shapley values, while the risk tools support
  historical replay, rolling backtests, stochastic simulation and
  sequence-risk analysis. The simulator also supports inflation-aware
  projections, goal-seek calculations, multi-fund portfolios and
  auditable reporting. Indian resident-individual capital-gains
  treatment is modelled for the supported scope. The numerical engine
  is cross-checked against independently written reference simulators
  over tens of thousands of generated investment plans. The software
  is intended for simulation and education rather than market
  forecasting or investment advice.

